Danus-R adds an experimental V8 scientific research workflow, including
adaptive Researcher/Reviewer/Experimenter role dispatch, Host-owned
experimental validation, frozen inputs and proposals, Reviewer issue
resolution, an audit event log, and targeted sandbox resource protections.
Modifications relative to the upstream repository can be traced through
the Git history included with this distribution.

The upstream Danus publication and mathematical proof-search results are
not Danus-R publications or scientific findings. Danus-R's three local
pilot outcomes are exploratory and have not been established as independent
public benchmarks. Other dependencies retain their own applicable licenses.
